module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.DegreeDefs
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.SectionwiseQuotient

/-!
# The quotient by a graded ideal against the clauses of Tags 0801 and 0802

`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/Quotient.lean` constructs the quotient
`𝒜/ℐ` of a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra by a graded ideal, its quotient homomorphism, and
the closed immersion `Proj_S(𝒜/ℐ) ⟶ Proj_S(𝒜)`. This file reads those against the clauses the
statements of Tags 0801 and 0802 are written with.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.isQuotientByDegreeSubmodule_quotMk`: **the
  kernel clause of Tag 0802** — the kernel of the quotient by the graded ideal `ℱ𝒜` generated by
  a submodule of one homogeneous piece is `ℱ𝒜`, degreewise, on the sections over every affine
  open of the base.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0801](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0801)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0802](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0802)

## Not done here

No Stacks tag is claimed here. **Tag 0801's relative `iso` clause is proved**, downstream, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/VanishingPresentation.lean`: the
chart-level hypothesis the reductions of this file leave is discharged there by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwists.ker_eq_chartMap_ker`, and the whole of
`…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.VanishingIdealPresentation` is built as
`…RelativeProjTwists.vanishingIdealPresentation`, on no hypothesis beyond Tag 0801's own. Tag
0803 is registered with that presentation discharged in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/FiniteTypePresentationOffSupport.lean`.

What closed the clause, on top of the reductions here: the chart comparison
`…RelativeProjTwists.pullbackGlobalSections_degreeSection_eq_zero_iff`, which composes
`…RelativeProjTwists.TwistData.ψ_chart` with the base change of the unit `M ⟶ i_*i^*M` along an
arbitrary open immersion (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ChartUnit.app_unit_eq_zero_iff`) and with
`…RelativeProjTwists.restrictionHom_app_eq_zero_iff_restrictionToClosed`; the resulting equality
of homogeneous ideals `…RelativeProjTwists.sectionGradedIdeal_eq_idealOfClosedSubscheme`; and the
absolute case of Tag 0801 restated at an `AddSubgroup`-valued grading,
`Stacks.ProjChartKerQuotient.ker_eq_ker_projMap_quotientMk`.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal

attribute [local instance_reducible] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

universe u

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (𝒜 : SheafGradedAlgebra S) {d : ℤ} (ℱ : (𝒜.piece d).Submodule)

/-- **The kernel clause of Tag 0802.** The quotient of `𝒜` by the graded ideal `ℱ𝒜` generated by
a submodule of one homogeneous piece has, degreewise and on the sections over every affine open
of the base, exactly `ℱ𝒜` as its kernel.

The clause asks for the sections over an affine open; what
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.quotMkApp_app_eq_zero_iff` gives is the
sections over every open, the quotient homomorphism being a cokernel. -/
theorem isQuotientByDegreeSubmodule_quotMk
    (hqc : IsQuasicoherentQuotPieces 𝒜 (gradedIdealGeneratedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ)) :
    IsQuotientByDegreeSubmodule 𝒜 ℱ (quotMk 𝒜 (gradedIdealGeneratedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ) hqc) :=
  fun n U _ a =>
    quotMkApp_app_eq_zero_iff 𝒜 (gradedIdealGeneratedByDegree 𝒜 ℱ) n U a

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal

end
